Key insight: A definition-site freeze rule can be defined as: canonicalize the "definition sites" (a declared set of paths that define class semantics, excluding provenance/timestamps) into a normalized digest, and compare against the frozen base. For m04 a leaf changed (adm_mass.sign: "no sign is assumed..." → "m_ADM >= 0 by the positive mass theorem"), for m16 containment reversal (probably extension_predicate or regularity containment wording), m25 WCC completeness swap (in W fixture), m29 data domain contradiction (D2 definition "asymptotically flat initial data satisfying both constraint equations; the vacuum condition is not required of the data" vs base presumably "one-ended asymptotically flat vacuum initial data...").

Rather than hand-designing, the strongest approach is a *general* definition-site freeze: normalize the YAML by deleting provenance/timestamp fields and re-serializing, then compare with the base. But a full-document freeze would catch all mutations (including the earlier-caught ones) and by definition catch m04/m16/m25/m29. The interesting measurement is which *sites* to freeze to catch the four escapes with zero false positives on conforming controls.

Key subtlety: R-CAND-F (statement freeze) was vocabulary-free and content-based. For R-CAND-D, the natural definition: freeze the *semantic definition sites* — a declared path set: quantifiers.*, domains.*, extension_predicate.*, data_class.* (minus citation_status/locator/status), genericity.* (minus citation_status/status), topology.*, regularity.* — normalized in a way that ignores formatting/reordering/comments but catches content changes. Then measure:
- catch rate on the 4 reference escapes,
- catch rate on the union corpora escape sets,
- false positives on conforming controls (identity controls, comment prepends, re-serialization),
- which of the already-caught probes it also flags (additivity),
- and a "minimal site set" analysis: which subset of the freeze catches the 4.

Also must include the crucial control: legitimate "metadata-only" edits (timestamps, provenance, citation_status) must NOT be flagged. The extended controls from heldout09r (comment prepend, comment append, renamed identical copy, pyyaml re-sort) are perfect false-positive candidates.

